    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a lower-cased email uniqueness check to `POST /api/owners`, responding **409** on a clash, following the existing `RejectDuplicateTelephone` pattern exactly.\n\n**New files (each a small, single-method cohesive unit \u2014 no existing class grew):**\n- `RejectDuplicateEmail.java` \u2014 a step function that, after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` has lower-cased the request email, compares it against every existing owner's lower-cased email and throws when it matches. A request without an email is skipped.\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (\u2192 409).\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 sends `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`.\n- `...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring for the handler.\n\n**One edited file:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `rejectDuplicateEmail` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline right after `rejectDuplicateTelephone`.\n\nStructural impact is kept minimal: no existing function was modified (only YAML wiring re-pointed one `next:` line), so all the behaviour lives in new classes with `WMC_other = 0` and trivial cyclomatic complexity.",
